# OLS or WLS for two noisy straight-line series (seed 221, n = 40 each)

Both series are y = 2.5 + 0.8 x + e at x = 0..39 from `default_rng(221)`, A first, then B. Noise sd is 3 for A and 0.5 + 0.15 x for B. For each series: OLS or WLS, and slope and intercept with 95% CIs?

**Decision.** A: **OLS**. B: **WLS**, weights 1/(0.5 + 0.15 x)². CIs are t-based (38 df, residual scale estimated); the true values (2.5, 0.8) lie inside all chosen-method intervals.

| Series | Method | Intercept [95% CI] | Slope [95% CI] |
|---|---|---|---|
| A | OLS (chosen) | 3.100 [1.39, 4.82] | 0.755 [0.679, 0.831] |
| B | WLS (chosen) | 2.609 [1.99, 3.23] | 0.847 [0.777, 0.918] |
| B | OLS (comparison) | 3.002 [0.95, 5.06] | 0.825 [0.734, 0.916] |

